<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan buys March heavy naphtha at below $240/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys March heavy naphtha at below $240/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has bought through a tender 30,000 tonnes of heavy naphtha for March 11-20 delivery at $239-$240 per tonne on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender which sought the cargo for delivery to Kaohsiung, closed on February 4 and was awarded Wednesday.</p>
<p>CPC's last purchase of heavy naphtha was awarded at $242-$244 c-and-f for delivery February 1-15.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
